FUNCTION "GLUE SCALE LOGIC" : VOID
TITLE =Glue Scale: DP Read, ASCII Parse, Valve Control, Alarms FC155
// v0.11 - Simplified "Parse integer part" network: replaced the 7
//   duplicated digit-check blocks (Byte_0..Byte_6, one hand-unrolled
//   per byte, ~140 lines) with a single indirect-addressed loop over
//   Byte_0..Byte_5 plus a short unconditional block for Byte_6 - same
//   LAR1/+AR1/DBB[AR1,P#x.y] indirect-addressing idiom this project
//   already uses in FB1111/FB1112/FC130. Behavior is unchanged: leading
//   spaces are skipped until the first digit (FoundDigit latches once
//   set, matching v0.10), and Byte_6 - the field's last position - is
//   still always parsed unconditionally, space or not. Also dropped a
//   dead SET;=FoundDigit pair at the top that was immediately
//   overwritten by the following CLR;=FoundDigit two lines later.
//
// v0.12 changes vs v0.11 - synced against DB105 v0.3 (see that block's
//   changelog, and DB105_Online_1.xps captured 2026-09-17):
//   - NEW network "Detect scale fault": the KWS CY300 sends a fixed
//     sentinel value (all 7 digits of the Byte_0-6 field filled, no
//     leading spaces - confirmed live at 5222222) instead of a real
//     reading when its measurement goes negative. GrossWeight_Actual is
//     compared against DB105's new NegativeUnderScore_Value constant
//     every scan; a match latches Alarm_ScaleFault. Exact REAL equality
//     is safe here specifically because both sides are integer-valued
//     (no fractional digit) and well under 2^24 - bit-exact in IEEE754
//     single precision, not the usual float-equality trap.
//   - "Skip valve/alarm update" network now also gates on Alarm_ScaleFault,
//     same as ParseError - a scale reporting its fault sentinel is not
//     a real weight, so the valve must not react to it (freezes at
//     last-good state, same as a garbled telegram) until an operator
//     acknowledges/resets Alarm_ScaleFault via HMI (not yet wired - see
//     README "Still open", same gap as the two existing alarms).
//   - Valve control network retargeted from the retired Setpoint_Fill/
//     Hysteresis pair to DB105's new Fill_Start_SP/Fill_Stop_SP: opens
//     below Fill_Start_SP, closes at/above Fill_Stop_SP directly - no
//     Hysteresis subtraction needed since the two setpoints already
//     define the deadband.
//
// v0.13 changes vs v0.12 - HMI alarm reset (per DB105 v0.4):
//   - NEW network "Reset latched alarms", placed after the SKIP: label
//     so it always runs every scan regardless of this scan's
//     ParseError/Alarm_ScaleFault skip state - a latched alarm must
//     stay resettable even while it's actively freezing the rest of
//     this block, otherwise Alarm_ScaleFault could never be cleared
//     once it fires (it would perpetually skip past its own reset).
//     Reads DB105.Reset_Alarms directly (level, not edge) - clears
//     Alarm_Overfill/Alarm_Underfill/Alarm_ScaleFault together while
//     TRUE; each alarm's own network re-latches next scan if its fault
//     condition is still actually present, so this can't mask a live
//     fault by holding the button down.
//
// v0.14 changes vs v0.13 - REAL -> INT for the scale weight/setpoints
//   (per DB105 v0.6 - Michou's call: the scale transaction doesn't need
//   fractional precision):
//   - Byte_8 (the scale's decimal digit) is no longer parsed at all -
//     #DecDigit and the REAL-math network that added it to
//     GrossWeight_Actual are gone. #IntPart (still DINT internally,
//     unchanged parse networks) is now stored directly into the INT
//     GrossWeight_Actual via a plain T - same DINT-to-narrower-type
//     truncation idiom already used elsewhere in this project (FC120's
//     Actual_Velocity, FB1111's StateCode/BadStreakCount).
//   - "Detect scale fault" now compares #IntPart directly (DINT, ==D)
//     against NegativeUnderScore_Value (DINT), BEFORE the truncation
//     into GrossWeight_Actual above - not the other way around. The
//     sentinel 5222222 does not fit in 16-bit INT range, so comparing
//     the already-truncated GrossWeight_Actual would compare a wrapped/
//     corrupted value and could never match the real sentinel again.
//     Order matters here: fault detection reads the wide temp, the INT
//     store is a separate, later step.
//   - Valve control, Overfill and Underfill networks switched from REAL
//     comparisons (<R/>=R/>R) to INT comparisons (<I/>=I/>I) to match
//     DB105's new field types. No logic/threshold change - same
//     open-below-Fill_Start_SP, close-at/above-Fill_Stop_SP behavior.
//
// v0.15 changes vs v0.14 - bridge to "HMI DB" (DB10), per Michou's call
//   to wire this here rather than in FC160 or a new block:
//   - NEW network "Sync HMI setpoints -> scale setpoints", placed first
//     (before the DPRD_DAT reads even complete/validate) - unconditional,
//     runs every scan regardless of ParseError/Alarm_ScaleFault, since
//     it's just mirroring operator-entered HMI input into the setpoints
//     FC155's own valve-control networks read; not tied to this scan's
//     telegram state at all.
//   - NEW network "Mirror parsed weight -> HMI DB", placed right after
//     "Store final weight" so it reflects this scan's just-computed
//     GrossWeight_Actual. Unconditional, same reasoning as
//     GrossWeight_Actual itself (see v0.12: it isn't held back on
//     ParseError either - it just gets whatever the byte parse
//     produced this scan).
//   - Only 3 of "HMI DB"'s and DB105's fields actually correspond by
//     meaning despite both having 5 consecutive INT fields at offsets
//     0/2/4/6/8: Actual_Glue_Weight<->GrossWeight_Actual (0.0),
//     Fill_Start_Weight_SP<->Fill_Start_SP (2.0), Fill_Stop_Weight_SP
//     <->Fill_Stop_SP (4.0). "HMI DB".Actual_Transfered_Weight/
//     Bottomer_Velocity (6.0/8.0) and DB105.AlarmLimit_Overfill/
//     AlarmLimit_Underfill (6.0/8.0) are unrelated fields that only
//     happen to share the same byte offsets - deliberately wired by
//     symbol name below, one field at a time, not as a block copy
//     across the matching address range.
//
// v0.16 changes vs v0.15 - extend the HMI bridge to the overfill/
//   underfill setpoints, per the physical "Glue InFeed Manager" touch
//   panel screen (has "Over Filled Weight"/"Under Filled Weight" fields
//   that had no DB10 backing at all until DB105 HMI DB v0.2):
//   - "Sync HMI setpoints -> scale setpoints" gains two more transfers:
//     "HMI DB".Overfill_Weight_SP -> AlarmLimit_Overfill, "HMI DB".
//     Underfill_Weight_SP -> AlarmLimit_Underfill. Same one-way,
//     unconditional pattern as Fill_Start_SP/Fill_Stop_SP - the touch
//     panel's own numeric-entry widget is the display of record for
//     what was last typed, so no mirror back is needed (matches why
//     Fill_Start_SP/Fill_Stop_SP were never mirrored back either).
VERSION : 0.16


VAR_TEMP
  RetVal1 : INT ;
  RetVal2 : INT ;
  IntPart : DINT ;
  CharVal : INT ;
  FoundDigit : BOOL ;
  LoopIndex : INT ;
END_VAR
BEGIN
NETWORK
TITLE =Sync HMI setpoints -> scale setpoints (unconditional, every scan)
// Only these fields correspond between "HMI DB" and DB105 - see v0.15/
// v0.16 changelogs for why the other same-offset fields must NOT be
// copied this way.
      L     "HMI DB".Fill_Start_Weight_SP;
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Fill_Start_SP;

      L     "HMI DB".Fill_Stop_Weight_SP;
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Fill_Stop_SP;

      L     "HMI DB".Overfill_Weight_SP;
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".AlarmLimit_Overfill;

      L     "HMI DB".Underfill_Weight_SP;
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".AlarmLimit_Underfill;

NETWORK
TITLE =Read 16-byte consistent block (IB272-287) via DPRD_DAT

      CALL "DPRD_DAT" (
           LADDR                    := W#16#110,
           RET_VAL                  := #RetVal1,
           RECORD                   := P#DB4.DBX0.0 BYTE 16);

NETWORK
TITLE =Read 4-byte consistent block (IB289-292) via DPRD_DAT

      CALL "DPRD_DAT" (
           LADDR                    := W#16#121,
           RET_VAL                  := #RetVal2,
           RECORD                   := P#DB4.DBX16.0 BYTE 4);

NETWORK
TITLE =Validate telegram - check RetVal and fixed markers (decimal poin

      L     #RetVal1; 
      L     0; 
      <>I   ; 
      L     #RetVal2; 
      L     0; 
      <>I   ; 
      OW    ; 
      L     "ABC3000A_DB".Byte_7; 
      L     B#16#2E; 
      <>I   ; 
      OW    ; 
      L     "ABC3000A_DB".Byte_9; 
      L     B#16#6B; 
      <>I   ; 
      OW    ; 
      L     "ABC3000A_DB".Byte_10; 
      L     B#16#67; 
      <>I   ; 
      OW    ; 
      =     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ParseError; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Parse integer part, Byte_0-5 - loop, skip leading spaces until f

      CLR   ; 
      =     #FoundDigit; 
      L     0; 
      T     #IntPart; 

      OPN   "ABC3000A_DB"; 
      LAR1  P#0.0; 

      L     6; 
LP1:  T     #LoopIndex; 

      L     DBB [AR1,P#0.0]; 
      L     B#16#20; 
      <>I   ; 
      S     #FoundDigit; 

      A     #FoundDigit; 
      JCN   ND1; 

      L     DBB [AR1,P#0.0]; 
      L     B#16#30; 
      -I    ; 
      T     #CharVal; 
      L     #IntPart; 
      L     10; 
      *D    ; 
      L     #CharVal; 
      ITD   ; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #IntPart; 

ND1:  +AR1  P#1.0; 

      L     #LoopIndex; 
      LOOP  LP1; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Parse integer part, Byte_6 - field's last position, always a dig

      L     "ABC3000A_DB".Byte_6; 
      L     B#16#30; 
      -I    ; 
      T     #CharVal; 
      L     #IntPart; 
      L     10; 
      *D    ; 
      L     #CharVal; 
      ITD   ; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #IntPart; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Detect scale fault - raw parsed integer matches the scale's negative-value sentinel (latching)
// Compares the wide #IntPart DINT temp, not GrossWeight_Actual - the
// sentinel 5222222 doesn't fit in 16-bit INT range, so this must run
// BEFORE #IntPart is truncated into the INT GrossWeight_Actual below.
      L     #IntPart;
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".NegativeUnderScore_Value;
      ==D   ;
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault;

NETWORK
TITLE =Store final weight - Byte_8's decimal digit is discarded, INT resolution is 1kg

      L     #IntPart;
      T     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual;

NETWORK
TITLE =Mirror parsed weight -> HMI DB (unconditional, for display)

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual;
      T     "HMI DB".Actual_Glue_Weight;

NETWORK
TITLE =Skip valve/alarm update if parse failed or scale fault latched t

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".ParseError; 
      O     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault; 
      JC    SKIP; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Valve control - open below Fill_Start_SP, close at/above Fill_St

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Valve_Open; 
      JC    CHKC; 

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual;
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Fill_Start_SP;
      <I    ;
      JC    OPEN;
      JU    VEND;

CHKC: L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual;
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Fill_Stop_SP;
      >=I   ;
      JC    CLOS;
      JU    VEND; 

OPEN: SET   ; 
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Valve_Open; 
      JU    VEND; 

CLOS: SET   ; 
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Valve_Open; 

VEND: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Overfill alarm - latching, set on exceed, no auto-reset here

      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual;
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".AlarmLimit_Overfill;
      >I    ;
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Overfill;

NETWORK
TITLE =Underfill check - start 5s settle timer on valve close (falling 

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Valve_Open_Prev; 
      AN    "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Valve_Open; 
      L     S5T#5S; 
      SD    T     50; 

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Valve_Open; 
      =     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Valve_Open_Prev; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Underfill alarm - latch if weight still below limit when timer e

      A     T     50; 
      JCN   SKPU; 
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".GrossWeight_Actual;
      L     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".AlarmLimit_Underfill;
      <I    ;
      S     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Underfill;
SKPU: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Exit point for parse-error skip

SKIP: NOP   0; 

NETWORK
TITLE =Reset latched alarms - HMI-driven, runs regardless of this scan'

      A     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Reset_Alarms; 
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Overfill; 
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_Underfill; 
      R     "GLUE SCALE CONTROL DB".Alarm_ScaleFault; 

END_FUNCTION

